      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo is a disordered BCC alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline alloy has a room-temperature compressive yield strength of about 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline alloy has limited room-temperature compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to replace 20–30% of the Mo content with Nb.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial replacement of Mo by Nb will produce a more uniform solid solution.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial replacement of Mo by Nb will diminish local electronegativity disparities.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial replacement of Mo by Nb will reduce local lattice distortion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced electronegativity differences will lower chemical pinning of dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower chemical pinning will facilitate dislocation slip.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced dislocation mobility will improve room-temperature compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo provides important room-temperature strengthening in the Hf-Mo-Nb-Ti-Zr alloy system.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Retaining most of the Mo while adding Nb will largely preserve the baseline alloy's strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-substituted alloy will show a significant increase in room-temperature compressive plastic strain.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744483::web::002::1_introduction",
        "PMC7512535::web::025::4_2_ta_and_w_effects_at_room_temperature"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-substituted alloy's yield strength will remain within approximately 5–10% of 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial strength-plasticity effect will occur only when 20–30% of the Mo content is replaced.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive Mo replacement may reduce Mo-driven strengthening.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive Mo replacement may cause the alloy to lose its disordered BCC structure.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The plasticity improvement and strength-retention limit will depend on substitution ratio and processing conditions.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
